WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.350
"History" is something that does not exist in space.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.810
Past, present, future...

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.900
These are subjective human concepts.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.110
Points on a limited axis of time.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.780
However,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.700
if humanity continues to seek out new places to populate,

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.120
the points may become a line.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.080
And the history of mankind may become a flower,

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.710
blooming throughout the universe.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.210
I'm sure you still have your royal obligations.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.420
But as Gruier, what will <i>you</i> do?

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.340
I don't know yet.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.690
I'm tired...

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.110
I get nervous in front of crowds.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.150
It's the same routine, but a different audience each time.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.570
Hey, we still have work today, right?

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.660
Let's see...

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.040
A delivery to the Stellar Military hospital ship?

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:31.500
A bio-container from a Galactic Empire biological research facility.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.340
Well, it's just a delivery.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.210
You can go home if you want.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.300
Really?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.380
A student's gotta study.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.840
We're gonna be busy next week though.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.300
A delivery to Schwarzberg,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.560
and a piracy job on the luxury liner Queen Esmeralda.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.560
You'll need to be in top shape, Captain.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.020
Okay, I'll let you guys handle the rest.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.230
See you later.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.190
Roger.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:28.770
Ta-dah!

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.230
These are adorable.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.940
Don't you think they'd look cute on the chest of your pirate uniform?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.940
Remember how I was customizing it before?

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.860
It was so fun

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.320
that I made a bunch of variations.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.200
I stayed up all night.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.120
All night?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:45.620
Yup.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:49.580
I want to be your personal stylist.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.330
You might be in the news a lot more, right?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.290
I don't think so...

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.260
I want to do what I can to help you.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.800
So if there's any outfit you'd like me to make, let me know.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:04.640
Thanks.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.600
Oh, yeah.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.100
I have to check in.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.220
Huh?

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:09.850
What?

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:10.480
What's up?

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.940
Normally, I receive a message from the Bentenmaru before lunch.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.940
Maybe they're busy?

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.900
I didn't think we were that busy today.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.610
I wonder if something happened.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.820
Still no word?

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.120
No.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.580
That's odd.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.160
They do it to keep tabs on you.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.290
It's strange that they'd forget.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.630
Maybe something happened.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.550
They called me?

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.590
Hello?

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.010
Yeah.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.390
Yup... Yup.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:48.890
One second...

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.060
Captain, it's an emergency.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:51.850
An emergency?

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.560
Hello?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.100
Marika?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:56.650
Misa?

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.110
What happened to your voice?

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.230
A cold...

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.440
More or less.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.570
The entire crew is in isolation.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.530
We're on the hospital ship.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.160
Isolation? Why?

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.500
Remember that cat-monkey bio-container?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.120
It appears there was a timer set to open it.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:20.810
Five of them were carrying an infectious disease with cold-like symptoms.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:25.050
It's a nasty bug that spread almost instantly through the ship's ventilation system.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:30.140
For now, the symptoms are just coughing and a fever.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.720
They said we're in no danger.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.730
How about you, Marika?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.350
You feeling okay?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:40.400
Captain, you okay?

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:44.490
Don't grow up to be bad people like us...

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:48.070
Hyakume, that didn't make any sense.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.410
I'm fine for now, I think.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.870
Good.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.370
So that's why you didn't check in.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.040
Sorry.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.540
The checkups took a while.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.380
What about our next job?

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.170
I don't think it's gonna happen.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.380
The Bentenmaru's been disinfected,

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.760
and we should recover in about a week.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:16.560
But someone planned to use this virus for some shady stuff.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.060
They aren't certain a vaccine will work.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:25.230
We can't go outside for at least two weeks, to make sure we're completely cured.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.490
Two weeks?!

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:27.530
That long?

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.910
So anyway, sorry,

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.280
but could you call the insurance company?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:40.210
You're the captain, and this is a good chance for you to start learning the business end.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.920
Sounds like trouble.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.920
Hey, Ririka,

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.180
Misa said to call the insurance company, but...

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.430
She wants you to call that ass, Harold?

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.930
Jeez.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:56.350
Just thinking about him makes me mad!

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.770
Ah! It's hot!

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.230
D-Did something happen?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:05.440
Harold, of the Harold Lloyd Insurance Union, and I don't get along.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.240
Once, I tried increasing the number of machine guns,

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.200
to make the performance flashier,

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.200
and he started whining about depreciation schedules.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.740
Plus, he charges a ton.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.040
They're basically mobsters.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.710
They take payments from both the cruise ships and the pirates.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:26.590
Naturally, pirates get into a lot of trouble, so they need insurance.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.300
I see...

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:29.760
Anyway,

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.260
be careful.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.760
He's a grownup and a skilled negotiator.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.220
Keep your wits, and don't give him the advantage.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.100
R-Right.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:45.770
Okay, let's try moving them.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.900
Grab the control stick.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.110
Hey, what's Marika doing?

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:54.430
Dunno.

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:56.990
Maybe she's doing some new pirate job in the club room?

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.450
Huh? Like what?

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.410
N-Nice to meet you.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.380
I-I'm Kato Marika, captain of the B-Bentenmaru.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.130
I'm Show, agent for the Harold Lloyd Insurance Union.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.720
What? You aren't Mr. Harold?

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.970
I took over five years ago.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.550
Misa didn't tell you?

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.560
I-I'm sorry!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.930
Don't be so nervous.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.730
I won't eat you.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:24.270
Right.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.400
Harold was a tough guy to get along with,

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.070
and he fought a lot with the pirates.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.950
He was on especially bad terms with Blaster Ririka.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.740
They'd get into fistfights.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.620
Unfortunately, I'm a pacifist.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.830
So I'd prefer to get along with everyone.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.830
Yes... I hope we can too.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.170
Then let's get to the point.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:52.170
We understand that the Bentenmaru's crew is in isolation.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.180
What about the Bentenmaru itself?

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.640
It's locked and on autopilot.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.140
The crew is expected to stay in isolation for two weeks.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.270
Unfortunately, that means we'll have to

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.390
cancel the Schwarzberg delivery

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.570
as well as the Queen Esmeralda attack.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.360
Understood.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.570
I'll make alternate arrangements for those two jobs.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.660
But the problem is what happens afterwards!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.330
I'm told that the isolation period is two weeks,

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:23.410
but that they aren't sure that the vaccine will work.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.420
And the hospital will want to get detailed treatment data.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.500
So they'll be in isolation for at least a month!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.170
A month?

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.960
That's obstruction of business!

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.470
It's more serious than that.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:37.890
What do you mean?

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:42.720
One month of no activity and the
Bentenmaru's pirate license will be revoked!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.930
What?!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:51.650
However, Captain, should you board the Bentenmaru and conduct normal pirate business during that time,

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.070
the license will be renewed!

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.900
Oh, good...

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.030
Wait, how am I supposed to run the whole thing myself?!

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.330
What should I do?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.370
I made you some coffee.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:07.830
Thanks.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.170
Ririka...

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:13.000
Prayer, kidnapping, and recruitment...

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.630
Which do you think is the best option?

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:16.840
You see...

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.990
The truth is...

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:20.800
You have three options.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.220
Option 1!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:27.060
Pray that the crew is released while your pirates license is still valid!

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:28.310
Option 2!

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:33.020
If you don't think you'll make it, you could rescue your crew from the hospital ship.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.360
Neither is very realistic.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.490
Then you have one option left.

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.690
Find yourself a new crew.

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:44.120
What? Find a new crew... How?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.160
Anyway...

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.000
You only need to complete one pirate job.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:54.460
What you choose is up to you, Captain!

00:10:56.450 --> 00:11:00.890
I've given it a lot of thought, and maybe recruitment would be the best option.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.430
I see.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:06.470
Where do you think I can find good sailors?

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.930
Maybe the floating airport?

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.980
You think a spaceship crew would come down to Earth?

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.690
You find sailors in a port, just as you always have.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:16.150
A port?

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:17.610
Here that would be...

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.700
Hmm... The relay station.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.970
Look, there's the girl who received that medal.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.390
That's the captain of the Bentenmaru!

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:05.450
Thank you for flying the New Okuhama Airport Relay Station Shuttle, flight 714.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.540
The control tower has just cleared us,

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.870
so we'll be taxiing to the runway for takeoff the shortly.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.750
Please fasten your seat belts, and remain seated.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.880
May I sit here?

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.170
G-Gruier!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:22.680
Did you follow me?

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:23.930
Yeah.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.340
Why?

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:28.890
First, you were using the club room
communicator for a long time yesterday.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:33.690
Additionally, Mami said you didn't go to work,

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.110
which means something's happening on the Bentenmaru.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.070
But still...

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:42.820
Do I need a reason to help a friend?

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:47.030
I'm not here as a member of the royal family,

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.030
but merely as Gruier.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.000
I want to help you.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.620
Should I not have come?

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.670
I appreciate it.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.420
But you're a princess. Just remember that!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.590
Of course.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.230
I wonder what Marika's doing.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.030
You don't think

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.900
she's enjoying being a normal high school girl for once?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.870
I hope she doesn't rest too long

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.330
and forget she's the captain.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.580
The same goes for us.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.080
I can't say it...

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.710
So this is the relay station?

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.670
It's my first time here.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:50.390
It isn't a place for the princess of a whole country to go.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.520
See? Everyone's looking at you.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.940
No, they're looking at you.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.150
I'm in disguise.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.320
I knew it. It's Captain Marika!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.110
She really is a high school girl.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:07.740
You should keep in mind how famous you are.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.580
You ought to disguise yourself
before you start looking for a crew.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.250
D-Disguise?

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.500
Leave it to me.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.210
Two suits would cost... about this much?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.090
T-That much?

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.840
You could get a nice one for this amount.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.550
Oh, that's inexpensive.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.800
G-Gruier...

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:36.770
I feel really weird...

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.480
It looks good on you.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:44.440
Even at the Sailor's Office downtown no one will recognize you.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:46.610
Why is the skirt so short?

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:47.900
Why can't I wear pants?

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.870
Wearing a pantsuit is beneath Captain Marika of the Bentenmaru!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.370
Why?

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.750
First, we should check the Sailor's Office databank.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:04.840
How many crew have handled a category-1 spaceship for three years or more?

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.670
That's too many.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:08.550
Let's narrow it down.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:14.050
Five years or more of actual experience,
and an Imperial Class-1 Navigator's license...

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.020
This is gonna take a while.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.100
Um, Marika,

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.190
as the Bentenmaru's captain,

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:26.360
what do you think is most important in your crew?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:28.190
What's most important?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.450
I've never thought about it before.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.700
When I became captain, the crew was already assembled.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:38.250
This might be a good chance to figure that out.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.090
What's most important, huh?

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:49.210
The Bentenmaru's a pretty easy workplace.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:51.050
I wonder why.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:54.090
What do you think the Bentenmaru's crew has going for them?

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.140
Technical skill, maybe?

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.680
And, let's see... Good personalities?

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:02.190
All right.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.060
But still...

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:07.150
I don't know how to judge a sailor.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.970
And therefore,

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.740
I'm counting on you.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:13.950
M-Me?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.830
I don't know anything about spaceships.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.580
That's okay!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.620
I'm counting on your ability to judge people.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.120
You've met a lot of people, right?

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.880
If I can be of help...

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:29.380
Okay, let's go find people!

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.150
We're not finding much.

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:59.620
Come to think of it, any sailors who are at port already have jobs.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:01.620
That's true.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.670
You like this one?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:09.840
W-What? I've no interest in a
shake with such a low-class color...

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.420
You wanna try it, right?

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:21.810
Ririka says the strange drinks in
places like this can be dangerous.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.520
I'll pass.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:25.230
Then, two of these.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.060
I can't be too picky,

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:32.320
but they're going to be on my ship.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.240
What's everyone doing, anyway?

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.030
Girls!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:41.120
I heard you were looking for sailors.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:41.990
Is that true?

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:43.450
Yes...

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.120
It's your lucky day, miss.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:51.340
We have people who know how to crew a ship right here.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:55.090
We'll work for cheap, so will you hire all of us?

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.380
Oh!

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.180
You don't look so hard up for work

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:01.640
that you'd take on a job without asking for details.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.100
You need an explanation?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:08.350
In space, no one cares so long as you have the skills.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.940
Naturally, I don't care.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.610
But I require a skilled crew.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:18.660
If you don't mind, would you tell me what kind of ship you pilot, Captain?

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.370
How'd you know I was the captain?

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.790
By your bearing, I think.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.620
You just had that look about you.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.130
I love it!

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.170
You're exactly as I'd heard.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.010
Dad, that's enough.

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:40.640
That's...

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.680
Chiaki!

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:44.930
Which means...

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:50.230
I am Kenjo Kurihara, captain of the pirate ship Barbalusa.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.230
So this is the Barbalusa.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:57.860
It looks as old as the Bentenmaru.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:01.240
Well, it's been modified a bit.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:05.490
Piloting with the newest stuff dulls your senses as a sailor.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.080
That's what my crew says.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.120
Do you have time for this?

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.460
Aren't you looking for crew for the Bentenmaru?

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.880
How did you know?

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.960
We have the same insurance company.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.180
I see. So you know everything.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:24.930
We're taking over the pirating of the Queen Esmeralda.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.140
You are?

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:30.270
Sorry. Thanks...

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.560
Well, we help each other when we're in trouble.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.940
So did you find anyone?

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.150
Nope.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.860
I talked to a few people and got turned down.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.320
I'm sure you did.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:43.660
Why?

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.990
Because I went around and told everyone

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:50.620
not to sign on if the captain of the Bentenmaru asked them.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:55.130
But I was in disguise!

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.420
You weren't fooling anyone.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.510
I thought it was perfect.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.590
But why would you do something mean like that?

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:03.800
It wasn't mean at all.

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:09.060
If random people began crewing the Bentenmaru, that'd be a problem.

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:13.440
That's why I came to interview them myself.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.020
But you didn't find any.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:20.570
Because I have no idea how to pick pirates.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.400
I couldn't help, either.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:27.700
There are a lot of ways to pick a crew.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.240
Skill.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:30.160
Personality.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.120
Strength.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.080
Each captain is different.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.750
That's what makes each ship unique.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:38.340
Captain Kato,

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:42.720
what is the most important thing you look for in a crew member?

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.010
Skill...

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:48.560
Personality...

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.310
A lot of things...

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.890
But most importantly,

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:55.690
whether I can trust them.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:20:57.650
I guess.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:03.950
But you can't trust someone you just met.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:08.280
Think about the people you know.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:12.330
There are lots of people you trust who can pilot a spaceship, right?

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.000
I understand!

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.710
You're so dense...

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:22.010
Oh, the yacht...

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:22.960
No way!

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:26.090
I heard about it, Marika!

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:28.850
The whole Bentenmaru crew is sick?

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.720
Aw, come on, girl...

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.100
Why didn't you tell us sooner?

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:36.310
Let's all do our best, okay?

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:37.060
Yeah!

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:38.900
That's right.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:40.020
I'm impressed, Miss Chiaki.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.440
You pulled everything together quickly.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.280
Not really.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:47.660
Either way, I'm happy for the chance to be with you again.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:55.330
Okay! So our next practice cruise will be pirating on the Bentenmaru.

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:55.830
Got it?

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.040
Right!

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.000
You can do anything as long as you've got the energy!

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:03.050
I hope this'll be okay...

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.260
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.470
Marika Goes Recruiting
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:12.470
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:17.980
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:20.980
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:24.360
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.450
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:30.490
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:39.420
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.300
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.130
How far?

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.800
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:54.430
Until the end.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.770
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.100
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:07.940
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:11.700
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.120
What should we do?

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.290
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:20.580
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:26.630
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.880
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:40.730
Kato Marika decides to take

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:43.400
the yacht club crew on her next pirating job.

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:46.480
By the time they're done, will the Bentenmaru

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:49.440
even be able to leave port successfully?

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:51.360
And what about the crew at the hospital?

